          %h2#definition Definition
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              An
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
              is
              %strong hypercomplete
              if the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitehead+theorem"} Whitehead theorem
              is valid in it.
            %p
              Equivalently: if all its object are
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercomplete+objects"} hypercomplete objects
          %h2#properties Properties
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              All
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphisms"} geometric morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to Y
              out of a hypercomplete
              = succeed "-topos" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              factor through the hypercompletion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat Y
              of
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            %p
              the inclusion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat Y \hookrightarrow Y
              induces an equivalence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Geom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mover
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi Geom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Geom(X,\hat Y) \stackrel{\simeq}{\to}
                    Geom(X,Y)
                    \\,.
          %p
            This is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, prop. 6.5.2.13
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
              which is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+dimension"} locally of homotopy dimension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \leq n
              for some finite
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ≥
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n\geq -1
              is hypercomplete.
          %p
            See the discussion at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+dimension"} homotopy dimension
            for details and further implications.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#hypercompletions Hypercompletions
          %p
            Every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            has a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercompletion"} hypercompletion
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+sub-%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} reflective sub-(∞,1)-category
            spanned by its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercomplete+objects"} hypercomplete objects
          %h3#EnoughPoints Enough points
          #PointOfAndInfinityTopos.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒳
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{X}
              an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
              %strong point
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒳
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{X}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphism"} geometric morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mo *
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi Grpd
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi p
                            %mo *
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi p
                            %mo *
                    %mi 𝒳
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (p^\ast \dashv p_*) \;\colon\;
                    \\infty Grpd
                    \\stackrel{\overset{p^\ast}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{p_\ast}{\to}}
                    \\mathcal{X}
            %p
              from
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi Sh
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \simeq Sh_\infty(\ast)
              to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒳
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{X}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒳
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{X}
              has
              %strong enough points
              if a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-morphism"} 1-morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒳
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{X}
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} equivalence
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒳
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{X}
              precisely if for all such points the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+image"} inverse image
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^\ast (f)
              (the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stalk"} stalk
              at the point) is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} equivalence
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              There exist
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-site"} 1-sites
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              such that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28n%2C1%29-topos"} (1,1)-topos
              of sheaves of sets on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              has
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point+of+a+topos"} enough points in the 1-topos sense
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-localic+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} 1-localic (∞,1)-topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒳
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{X}
              does not have enough points in the sense of def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PointOfAndInfinityTopos"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mi ℕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi z
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_{\mathbb{N}} \{x,z,y\}
              where the topology on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi z
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{x,z,y\}
              is generated by the two open subsets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{x,y\}
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{x,z\}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, Remark 6.5.4.7
            %p
              However, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercompletion"} hypercompletion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒳
                      %mo ∧
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{X}^\wedge
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒳
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{X}
              will have enough points. This follows from the fact that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒳
                      %mo ∧
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{X}^\wedge
              may be presented by the Jardine
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
              on the given site of definition, and that in the presence of enough 1-topos points the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalences"} weak equivalences
              of that model structure are the
              = succeed "-wise" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stalk"} stalk
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} model structure on simplicial sets
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
              for details.)
          .num_lemma
            %h6#observation Observation
            %p
              An
              = succeed "-topos" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point+of+a+topos"} enough points
              is hypercomplete. WARNING: See the remark above.
          %p
            This is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, remark 6.5.4.7
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              Recall from def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PointOfAndInfinityTopos"}
              that a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point+of+a+topos"} point of an (∞,1)-topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphism"} geometric morphism
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo :
                      %mn ∞
                      %mi Grpd
                      %mover
                        %munder
                          %mo →
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi p
                              %mo *
                        %mover
                          %mo ←
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi p
                              %mo *
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p : \infty Grpd \stackrel{\overset{p^*}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{p_*}{\to}} \mathbf{H}
            %p
              And by definition
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
              has
              %em enough points
              if a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : X \to Y
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+in+a+quasi-category"} equivalence
              if for all points
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stalk"} stalk
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mo *
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^* f
              is an equivalence in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
            %p
              But if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected"} connected
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mo *
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^* f
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitehead%27s+theorem"} Whitehead's theorem
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mo *
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^* f
              is an equivalence.
            %p
              So in an
              = succeed "-topos" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              = succeed "-connected" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %h2#nonexamples Non-examples
          %h3#goodwillie_jet_toposes
            Goodwillie
            = succeed "-jet" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo &gt;
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \gt 1
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Goodwillie+n-jet+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-toposes"} Goodwillie n-jet (∞,1)-toposes
            are generically far from being hypercomplete.
          %h2#models Models
          %h3#ModelCategory In terms of model category theory
          %p
            Hypercomplete
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stack"} ∞-stack
            = succeed "es" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} presented
            by the local
            = succeed "-Jardine" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andre+Joyal"} Joyal
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
            over all
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercover"} hypercover
          %p
            If the underlying ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sheaves"} sheaf
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            has
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point+of+a+topos"} enough points
            = succeed "wise" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stalk"} stalk
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} model structure on simplicial sets
          %p
            Contrary to that one can consider local models by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} left Bousfield localization
            of the global
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
            only at
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+cover"} Cech cover
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-categories of (∞,1)-sheaves
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mrow
                        %mi inj
                        %mo ,
                        %mi loc
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C^{op}, sSet]_{inj,loc}
              for the Joyal-Jardine
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} local model structure on simplicial presheaves
              (whose weak equivalence are morphisms that induce isomorphisms on homotopy-sheaves).
            %p
              The
              = succeed "-topos" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercompletion"} hypercompletion
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-sheaves
              on
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mrow
                        %mi inj
                        %mo ,
                        %mi loc
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∘
                    %mo ≃
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Sh
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn ∞
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ^
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    ([C^{op}, sSet]_{inj,loc})^\circ
                    \\simeq
                    \\widehat{ Sh_{(\infty,1)}(C)}
                    \\,.
          %p
            This is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, prop. 6.5.2.14
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              The strategy is to form the localization in a 2-step process, where we first just form the Cech-localization, and then from that the full hypercompletion. For that notice that among the weak equivalences in the Joyal-Jardine
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} local model structure on simplicial presheaves
              are in particular the ordinary covering
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sieve"} sieve
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S(\{U_i\}) \hookrightarrow j(U)
              (here
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
              is the
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
              = succeed "in" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cover"} cover
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to U\}
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %p
              since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is an ordinary category, the simplicial presheaves
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S(\{U_i\})
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j(U)
              have vanishing presheaves of homotopy groups in positive degree, while they coindide with their
              = succeed "-presheaves." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheafification"} sheafification
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S(\{U_i\})
              is isomorphic to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j(U)
              = succeed "-presheaves" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0
              = succeed "-presheaves." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S(\{U_i\}) \to j(U)
              is a Joyal-Jardine weak equivalence.
            %p
              We will now first localize with respect to these morphisms to obtain the Cech-localization whose fibrant objects are
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-sheaves
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+homotopy+groups+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-categorical homotopy sheaves
              in terms of which
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercompletion"} hypercompletion
              is defined.
            %p
              To start with, as discussed at
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-presheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-presheaves
              we have that the global model structure presents the
              = succeed "-presheaves:" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi inj
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∘
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi PSh
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    ([C^{op}, sSet]_{inj})^\circ \simeq PSh_{(\infty,1)}(C)
                    \\,.
            %p Observe that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  every simplicially constant object is fibrant in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mi op
                        %mo ,
                        %mi sSet
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mi inj
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C^{op}, sSet]_{inj}
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  hence since every object is cofibrant, the morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S(\{U_i\}) \to j(U)
                  is in
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msup
                            %mi C
                            %mi op
                          %mo ,
                          %mi sSet
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mi inj
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ∘
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ([C^{op}, sSet]_{inj})^\circ
              %li
                %p
                  under the abovee identification it is an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-monomorphism
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi PSh
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn ∞
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh_{(\infty,1)}(C)
                %p (discuss this bit in more detail…).
            %p
              Therefore the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+localization"} topological localization
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi PSh
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh_{(\infty,1)}(C)
              at these monomorphisms, i.e. the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-sheaves
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is presented by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} left Bousfield localization
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mrow
                        %mi inj
                        %mo ,
                        %mi cov
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C^{op}, sSet]_{inj,cov}
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi inj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C^{op}, sSet]_{inj}
              at the covering subfunctors
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S(\{U_i\}) \to j(U)
            %p
              By the above remark, the Joyal-Jardine localization
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mrow
                        %mi proj
                        %mo ,
                        %mi loc
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C^{op}, sSet]_{proj,loc}
              that we are after is a further localization of this Cech localization : we have the bottom row in the following diagram, and want to see that the top left corner is as indicated:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi Sh
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %mn ∞
                                    %mo ,
                                    %mn 1
