          %h3#in_classical_topos_theory In classical topos theory
          %p
            In classical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos+theory"} topos theory
            literature frequently
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+object"} simplicial object
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            are considered, with acyclic fibrations taken to be those morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Y
                    %mo •
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y_\bullet \to X_\bullet
            such that for all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horn"} horn
            inclusions the induced morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Y
                        %mrow
                          %mo ∂
                          %mi Δ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %msup
                    %mi Y
                    %mrow
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (X^{\Delta[n]} \to X^{\partial \Delta[n]} \times_{Y^{\partial \Delta[n]}} Y^{\Delta[n]})
          %p
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
            in the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
          %p See for instance page 17 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"}> Ieke Moerdijk
              ,
              %em Classifying spaces and classifying topoi
              (LNM 1616)
          %blockquote
            %p
              (and it looks like this is the discussion planned for part E of the
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Elephant"} Elephant
          %p
            For
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} sheaf toposes
            epimorphism means
            = succeed "-wise" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stalk"} stalk
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+fibrant+objects"} category of fibrant objects
            as defined in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BrownAHT"} BrownAHT
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibration"} Kan fibration
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
            of this
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopical+category"} homotopical category
            is the same as that of the Joyal-Jardine
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
            in the presence of enough points (since in both cases weak equivalences are the stalkwise weak equivalences), hence is the same as the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} homotopy category of the hypercomplete (∞,1)-topos
          %p
            For more discussion of how this classical definition interplays with other definitions see also
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} homotopy groups in an (∞,1)-topos
          %h2#references References
          %p
            The notion of hypercompleteness appears as
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
              \-completeness
            in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bertrand+Toen"} Bertrand Toen
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gabriele+Vezzosi"} Gabriele Vezzosi
              %em Segal topoi and stacks over Segal categories
              , Proceedings of the
              %p
                Program Stacks, Intersection theory and Non-abelian Hodge Theory, MSRI, Berkeley, January-May 2002 (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0212330"}> arxiv:math/0212330
                ).
          %p
            The notion of hypercomplete
            = succeed "-toposes" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} Higher Topos Theory
